# build output
dist/
# generated types
.astro/

# dependencies
# Keep this project outside ~/Desktop and ~/Documents. Both are iCloud-synced on
# this machine, and syncing node_modules is what made `astro dev` unusable: iCloud
# had evicted ~94% of it to the cloud (429MB logical, 24MB on disk), so every
# dependency read blocked on a download and the dev server sat at 0.4% CPU for
# minutes without ever binding its port. It now lives in ~/Projects, which iCloud
# does not touch.
#
# A `node_modules.nosync` symlink was tried first and did not survive — iCloud
# resolves symlinks into real directories, which put the deps straight back under
# sync. The entry stays ignored in case one gets recreated.
node_modules
node_modules.nosync/

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

